Below is a minimal pair of *SEARCH/REPLACE* edits that add full support for all of the common multi‐character integer literal suffixes (ll, LL, ull, ULL, llu, LLU, etc.) in both the decimal‐style and the hex/exponent‐style variants.  

We only touch the two number‐variants in `src/languages/c-like.js` — nothing else changes.

```javascript
### src/languages/c-like.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
      {
        begin: '(-?)\\b([\\d\\']+(\\.[\\d\\']*)?|\\.[\\d\\']+)(u|U|l|L|ul|UL|f|F|b|B)'
      },
=======
      {
        // allow all common C/C++ suffix combinations: ll, LL, ull, ULL, llu, LLU, etc.
        begin: '(-?)\\b([\\d\\\']+(\\.[\\\']*)?|\\.[\\\']+)(?:u|U|l|L|ul|UL|ll|LL|ull|ULL|llu|LLU|f|F|b|B)'
      },
>>>>>>> REPLACE

