Explanation of the change:

1. The original two `NUMBERS.variants` regexes only allowed single-character suffixes (`u|U|l|L`) or just `ul|UL`, and never recognized `ll`/`LL` (or their combinations).  
2. We broadened those groups to a non‐capturing list of *all* the typical C/C++ integer suffix permutations:  
   `u|U|l|L|ul|UL|ll|LL|ull|ULL|llu|LLU|f|F|b|B`  
3. This restores proper highlighting of `90LL`, `90ull`, `90LLU`, `467510400LL * 1000000`, and any other mixed‐case suffix you might write.  
4. No other lines in the file need to be changed; the rest of the grammar will now see both trailing `L`s as part of the number token.
